Z||000000||87FieroGTx||08-05-2001||03:20 PM||||Q's on painting a spoiler?<P> I just got done with my 5th coat of paint on my new spoiler, What now? Clearcoat?<P> Should I clearcoat it right after I do the last coat of red?<P> Sand befor clear? don't sand?<P> Once I clear coat it what then?||||reg||1
Z||000001||87FieroGTx||08-05-2001||03:22 PM|||| Oh.. I'me using rattlecans <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> I just want to git it lookn good till I can git a pro job, No jokes plz)||||reg||1
Z||000002||maryjane||08-05-2001||04:04 PM||||Boombastic has a pretty detailed guide on his web page. You will need acrobat reader I believe.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-05-2001||06:49 PM||||nothing wrong with rattle cans, i use em myself. if its a single stage paint your done. if its basecoat, it has to be cleared. let the base dry for an hour or so then clear it. dont sand, or even touch the basecoat without the clear. when you do clear it it will have streaks or your fingerprints in it.||||reg||1
