Z||000008||KRMFiero||08-06-2001||01:42 PM||||Just so you know most Spray paints already have like a built in clear coat so you dont need to put it on.<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||08-06-2001||05:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KRMFiero:<BR><B>Just so you know most Spray paints already have like a built in clear coat so you dont need to put it on.<P>Kyle</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>thats ONLY if its single stage paint. Most of those all use the clear as a 'carrier' to suspend metallic colors. clear carrier in solid colors is just to make the paint cheaper (ie-clears cheaper than red) If its a basecoat color, you must put clear over it or it will not hold up, wont have any gloss.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||bad911||08-07-2001||12:41 PM||||blayde8 thanks for the link... those guys ROCK!<P>Roger, are the single stage paints label so? How to tell single-stage vs basecoat paint and a quality one from a cheapie? thanks.<P>[This message has been edited by bad911 (edited 08-07-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by bad911 (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||rogergarrison||08-07-2001||12:54 PM||||the can should be labeled BASECOAT if it is. If its not labeled its prob single stage. If your not sure ask, if not then youll know when you spray it. basecoat will dry completely flat-no gloss at all.||||reg||1
Z||000012||gt boy||08-07-2001||08:22 PM||||the one trick i learned on how to make a "spray can" paint job look good is ...i know this sound dangerous and probably is ....but i always fill a pail with hot tap water(not boiling!!)and let the can of paint sit  in there for at least 15mins, shaking the can often to heat all the paint.  what this does is it allows the paint to be sprayed on in really thin coats and the paint blends in real nice with each passing spray stroke.<P>this is a trick my 'ol man taught me and it works really well.||||reg||1
Z||000013||rogergarrison||08-07-2001||09:10 PM||||yes, that works, it increases the pressure slightly in the can.||||reg||1
